### Tested versions

Reproduceable in: 4.6-stable, 4.5-stable (Windows)
Not yet tested: Linux, macOS

### System information

Godot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8183) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.34 GiB memory

### Issue description

Using the `--rendering-driver` command line flag overrides whatever rendering method is set in the project settings.

You can work around this by also using the `--rendering-method` flag.

This affected me because I was telling players to override the default rendering driver in some cases if they're having compatibility issues with Vulkan. I told them to use `--rendering-driver d3d12` to do this, but that caused some game objects to render incorrectly. I did not realise that the cause of those graphical issues was that the wrong rendering method was being used.

In `main.cpp`, in function `Main::setup`, the simplified logic is:

```
// read command line flags

if (!rendering_driver.is_empty()) {
    // use rendering method provided on command line

    if (rendering_method.is_empty()) {
        // default to dummy, gl_compatibility, or forward_plus, depending on rendering driver
    }
}

if (rendering_method.is_empty()) {
    // read ProjectSettings to determine rendering method
    // this code will never be reached if --rendering-driver was used
}
```

Link to relevant code:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0cd4a62f3b6349e5060f9fe95e473c670d7d2e22/main/main.cpp#L2517
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0cd4a62f3b6349e5060f9fe95e473c670d7d2e22/main/main.cpp#L2577

IMO this is a bug unless this behaviour were to be mentioned in the documentation of the `--rendering-driver` flag.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Open a project with rendering method set to mobile.
2. Export a Windows build.
3. Run it from the command line with `game.exe`, you should see "Forward Mobile" on the second line of output.
3. Run it from the command line with `game.exe --rendering-driver vulkan`, you should see "Forward+" on the second line of output.

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

Not project-specific, as far as I can tell.
